# Data and model artefacts - far too large for git, and all reproducible.
#   Detection.v1-cardd.yolov11/  360 MB  the raw Roboflow export (re-downloadable)
#   dataset/                     160 MB  regenerate with: python tools/prepare_dataset.py
#   dataset.zip                  154 MB  regenerate by re-zipping dataset/
# Sizes measured 2026-08-31. dataset/ and dataset.zip were ~384/344 MB before the leak fix,
# which dropped the export's 10,000 augmented files to 3,933 distinct photographs.
Detection.v1-cardd.yolov11/
dataset/
dataset.zip
# The checkpoint is ~77 MB and regenerable from notebooks/train_colab.ipynb, so it is
# not tracked - but keep weights/README.md, which says where to put it.
weights/*
!weights/README.md
runs/

# Sample photographs picked out of dataset/images/test for manual testing.
# Derived from the excluded Roboflow export, and reproducible in seconds by
# picking any image from dataset/images/test - so there is nothing to gain from
# committing them. sample_uploads/README.md is kept, because it documents the
# test runs and the numbers they should produce.
sample_uploads/*
!sample_uploads/README.md

# Environment
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Django
# SQLite writes two sidecar files alongside the database in write-ahead-log mode.
# They hold committed-but-not-yet-checkpointed pages, so committing them would
# put a fragment of one machine's database into everyone else's checkout.
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-wal
db.sqlite3-shm
media/
staticfiles/
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Left behind when a file is deleted while a FUSE mount still has it open.
# Nothing to do with the project, and the name changes every time.
.fuse_hidden*

# Claude Code per-machine config. settings.local.json holds ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN
# in cleartext, so it must never be committed - this repo is on GitHub.
# .claude/settings.json (shared, no secrets) is deliberately NOT ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
